File: bltzread.info,  Node: The word API,  Next: Hooks,  Up: Extending bltzread

13.1 The word API
=================

A word is an overlay in the buffer, with the properties ‘bltzread-form’
(the lowercased spelling), ‘bltzread-key’ (what its level is tracked
under: the form, or the basic word under ‘lemma’) and ‘bltzread-level’
(1 to 5, or ‘ignored’).

‘(bltzread-words)’
     The live word overlays of the buffer, in text order.
‘(bltzread-word-at &optional pos)’
     The word at POS, or nil.
‘(bltzread-require-word)’
     The word at point, or a ‘user-error’.
‘(bltzread-word-overlays beg end)’
     The words between two positions.
‘(bltzread-unknown-word-p ov)’
     Non-nil if the word is at or below ‘bltzread-unknown-max-level’.
‘(bltzread-first-unknown-between beg end)’
     Position of the first unknown word in the stretch, or nil.
‘(bltzread-set-level level)’
     Command: set the word at point.  ‘bltzread-increment-level’,
     ‘bltzread-decrement-level’ and ‘bltzread-ignore’ are commands too.
‘bltzread-annotate’, ‘bltzread-toggle-colors’, ‘bltzread-set-language’
     Commands.
‘bltzread-popup-visible-p’, ‘bltzread-popup-anchor’, ‘bltzread-dismiss-popup’, ‘bltzread-close-popup’, ‘bltzread-popup-hide’
     Ask about and close the card.
‘bltzread-offer-record’
     Ask once whether to record a session, as when a buffer is killed.
‘bltzread-finish-session’, ‘bltzread-mark-range-known’
     Commands that record a session.
‘bltzread-lookup’, ‘bltzread-popup-at-point’, ‘bltzread-note’
     Commands on the word at point.
‘bltzread-when-read-only’
     See _Changing the keys_.

   The old private names ‘bltzread--overlay-at’,
‘bltzread--require-word’, ‘bltzread--word-overlays’,
‘bltzread--unknown-p’ and ‘bltzread--all-words’ remain as obsolete
aliases.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Hooks,  Next: Seams,  Prev: The word API,  Up: Extending bltzread

13.2 Hooks
==========

All of them are options too.

‘bltzread-level-change-functions’
     Abnormal hook with ‘KEY FORM OLD NEW’ when the level of a word
     changes, in the buffer.  It runs once per key whose level changed
     (FORM is one of its spellings), not when words are first read in.
‘bltzread-lookup-functions’
     Abnormal hook with ‘KEY FORM LEVEL’ when a word counts as looked up
     (once per word and session).
‘bltzread-session-finished-functions’
     Abnormal hook with the history entry, a plist with ‘:time :buffer
     :beg :end :words :counted :promoted :queued’, after a session was
     recorded.
‘bltzread-after-annotate-hook’
     Normal hook after the words were (re)read.
‘bltzread-popup-show-hook’, ‘bltzread-popup-hide-hook’
     Normal hooks when a card is shown or hidden.
‘bltzread-popup-scroll-hook’
     Normal hook, with the window selected, after the card scrolled the
     window to make room.  A package that follows the window start can
     use it to tell this scroll from the user's.
‘bltzread-review-after-apply-hook’
     Normal hook after the review was applied.

   Example, a log of every level change:

     (add-hook 'bltzread-level-change-functions
               (lambda (_key form old new)
                 (message "%s: %s -> %s" form old new)))


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Seams,  Next: The rows of the card,  Prev: Hooks,  Up: Extending bltzread

13.3 Seams
==========

Four options replace one piece of machinery each.  The defaults call
bltzr and sdcv.

‘bltzread-tokenizer-function’
     Called with ‘BEG END LANG’; returns a list of ‘(BEG END FORM)’ in
     text order, FORM lowercased.
‘bltzread-lemmatizer-function’
     Called with ‘LANG SPELLINGS’; returns an ‘equal’ hash table of
     spelling to list of basic words.
‘bltzread-language-detect-function’
     Called with a text; returns a language code or nil.
‘bltzread-dictionary-function’
     Called with ‘LANG WORDS’; returns a string, a list of strings or
     nil.
‘bltzread-known-writer-function’
     Called with ‘LANG ENTRIES TARGET’, ENTRIES being ‘(FORM . LEMMA)’;
     returns ‘(FILE . ADDED)’.

   With these a different tokenizer, a dictionary in a web service or
another place for the known words need no change to bltzread.

* Menu:

* The dictionary entry convention::


File: bltzread.info,  Node: The dictionary entry convention,  Up: Seams

13.3.1 The dictionary entry convention
--------------------------------------

An entry is one string: the name of the dictionary, a newline, then the
text, which may be HTML.  For example ‘"Polish-English\n<span
class’\"trans\">building</span>"‘. The name is shown dimmed
(=bltzread-popup-dict-name’) and is what ‘bltzread-dict-filters’
matches.  An entry with no name starts with the newline.  Return a list
of such strings for several entries, which ‘d’ cycles.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: The rows of the card,  Next: Recipes,  Prev: Seams,  Up: Extending bltzread

13.4 The rows of the card
=========================

‘bltzread-popup-row-functions’ is a list of functions, called in order
with a word overlay and FULL (non-nil for a long entry from a lookup);
each returns a list of strings, possibly none.  The built-in ones are
‘bltzread-card-title-rows’, ‘bltzread-card-status-rows’,
‘bltzread-card-note-rows’, ‘bltzread-card-entry-rows’,
‘bltzread-card-gloss-rows’ and ‘bltzread-card-hint-rows’.  Reorder,
remove or add:

     (defun my-card-frequency-row (ov _full)
       (list (format "seen %d times" (my-count (overlay-get ov 'bltzread-form)))))

     (setq bltzread-popup-row-functions
           (append (butlast bltzread-popup-row-functions)
                   '(my-card-frequency-row bltzread-card-hint-rows)))

   The hints row is made from ‘bltzread-popup-hints’, an alist of
‘(COMMAND . LABEL)’; add your own commands there, buffer-locally if you
like.


