13.5.1 A quiet mode
-------------------

Only the card, no colours, no level keys, nothing counted by hand:

     (setq-local bltzread-no-colors t)
     (setq-local bltzread-popup-row-functions
                 '(bltzread-card-title-rows bltzread-card-gloss-rows))


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Always show level 5 in colour,  Next: Wiring subtle,  Prev: A quiet mode,  Up: Recipes

13.5.2 Always show level 5 in colour
------------------------------------

The fifth level has the empty face ‘bltzread-level-5’.  Give it a colour
with ‘M-x customize-face’, or point ‘bltzread-level-faces’ at another
face.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Wiring subtle,  Prev: Always show level 5 in colour,  Up: Recipes

13.5.3 Wiring subtle
--------------------

subtle plays audio or video in mpv and shows its subtitles as text.
Once subtle is loaded, bltzread connects itself (file
‘bltzread-subtle.el’): blitz playback follows the first unknown word of
each cue and opens its card by itself (and closes the card of the word
before), the scrolling the card makes does not count as the user's
scrolling, and the card's hint row shows the key of
‘subtle-blitz-toggle’ during a subtle session.  Nothing else is needed
for those.  The rest is your choice:

     (setq bltzread-range-farthest-source #'subtle-played-through-position
           bltzread-range-start-function  #'subtle-played-start-position)

     (add-hook 'subtle-buffer-setup-hook
               (lambda ()
                 (when (= subtle-track-index 0)
                   (setq bltzread-language subtle-language)
                   (bltzread-mode 1))))

     (add-hook 'subtle-pause-hook
               (lambda () (when bltzread-mode (bltzread-avy-unknown))))

   The first sets reading credit to what was played; the second turns
the mode on for the first subtitle track only; the third puts avy hints
on the unknown words when you pause.  Keep ‘subtle-scroll-style’ at
‘paged’: continuous scrolling carries a word away while you look it up.
The first load of a long transcript takes a moment because bltzr is
called once for all its words.  subtle's own settings let a card hold
the page and let ‘q’ close it first; they use ‘bltzread-popup-visible-p’
and ‘bltzread-dismiss-popup’.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Limits,  Prev: Extending bltzread,  Up: Top

14 Limits
*********

   • Single words only; phrases are not tracked.
   • Basic forms come from bltzr and are looked up again in each Emacs
     session.
   • Nothing is shared between languages.
   • The levels are five and fixed.


